{"title":"Career Roadmap — Design Researcher","role":"Design Researcher","summary":"A Design Researcher investigates people, communities, organisations, systems and environments to understand problems and generate evidence that informs better design decisions.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Des (Bachelor of Design)","Course":"Design for Social Innovation / Sustainable Design"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Design Researcher investigates people, communities, organisations, systems and environments to understand problems and generate evidence that informs better design decisions."},{"type":"p","text":"In social innovation and sustainable design, the role goes beyond conventional product research. A design researcher may study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"User behaviour and needs"},{"text":"Communities and social systems"},{"text":"Sustainability challenges"},{"text":"Environmental behaviour"},{"text":"Public services"},{"text":"Circular economy systems"},{"text":"Accessibility and inclusion"},{"text":"Rural and urban challenges"},{"text":"Consumer behaviour"},{"text":"Sustainable consumption"},{"text":"Organisational processes"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The researcher converts observations and evidence into insights, opportunities, design requirements and strategic recommendations."},{"type":"h","text":"Typical Route"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Des Design for Social Innovation / Sustainable Design","Research Methods + Sustainability","Research Internship / Field Research","Junior Design Researcher / Research Assistant","Design Researcher","Senior Design Researcher","Lead / Strategic Design Researcher","Research Lead / Design Strategy Director"]}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Stage","Primary Focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1"},{"text":"Design fundamentals + observation"}],[{"text":"Year 2"},{"text":"Research methods + human-centred design"}],[{"text":"Year 3"},{"text":"Field research + sustainability systems"}],[{"text":"Year 4"},{"text":"Strategic research + major research project"}],[{"text":"0–2 years"},{"text":"Research Assistant / Junior Design Researcher"}],[{"text":"2–5 years"},{"text":"Design Researcher"}],[{"text":"5–8 years"},{"text":"Senior Design Researcher"}],[{"text":"8+ years"},{"text":"Research Lead / Design Strategy Lead"}]]}]},{"heading":"What to Build Each Year","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Design & Observation Foundations"},{"type":"p","text":"The first year should establish the ability to observe, document and interpret real-world problems."},{"type":"h","text":"Learn"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Design fundamentals"},{"text":"Visual communication"},{"text":"Observation"},{"text":"Sketching"},{"text":"Photography"},{"text":"Documentation"},{"text":"Design history"},{"text":"Human-centred design"},{"text":"Basic sustainability concepts"},{"text":"Introduction to social innovation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Develop Observation Skills"},{"type":"p","text":"Practice documenting:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"How people use products"},{"text":"How people navigate spaces"},{"text":"How resources are consumed"},{"text":"Where users experience difficulties"},{"text":"How communities solve problems themselves"},{"text":"What behaviours repeat in everyday life"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year-1 Project"},{"type":"h","text":"Everyday Sustainability Observation Study"},{"type":"p","text":"Choose one issue such as:"},{"type":"p","text":"Household food waste"},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Current behaviour"},{"text":"User frustrations"},{"text":"Existing solutions"},{"text":"Waste points"},{"text":"Opportunities for improvement"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Produce:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Observation notes"},{"text":"Photographs"},{"text":"User profiles"},{"text":"Problem map"},{"text":"Initial insights"},{"text":"Design opportunities"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — Design Research Methods"},{"type":"p","text":"Year 2 should establish formal research capability."},{"type":"h","text":"Qualitative Research"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"User interviews"},{"text":"Contextual interviews"},{"text":"Observation"},{"text":"Ethnographic research"},{"text":"Diary studies"},{"text":"Focus groups"},{"text":"Participatory research"},{"text":"Expert interviews"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Quantitative Research"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Surveys"},{"text":"Sampling"},{"text":"Descriptive statistics"},{"text":"Cross-tabulation"},{"text":"Basic data analysis"},{"text":"Questionnaire design"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The goal is not to become a statistician but to understand when and how quantitative evidence should support design decisions."}]},{"heading":"Research Process","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A design researcher should understand the complete process:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Research Question","Research Planning","Participant Selection","Data Collection","Interview / Observation","Data Organisation","Coding & Analysis","Patterns","Insights","Opportunity Areas","Design Recommendations","Prototype / Intervention","Testing","Evaluation"]},{"type":"p","text":"The critical difference is:"},{"type":"p","text":"Research data is not automatically an insight."},{"type":"p","text":"A researcher must interpret evidence and explain why it matters for the design problem."}]},{"heading":"Year 3 — Social Innovation & Sustainability Research","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Year 3 should move toward complex real-world systems."},{"type":"h","text":"Study"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Systems thinking"},{"text":"Social innovation"},{"text":"Circular economy"},{"text":"Sustainable development"},{"text":"Behaviour change"},{"text":"Environmental psychology"},{"text":"Inclusive design"},{"text":"Participatory design"},{"text":"Community design"},{"text":"Service design"},{"text":"Policy and social systems"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Systems Thinking"},{"type":"p","text":"Instead of asking:"},{"type":"p","text":"\"How can we design a better product?\""},{"type":"p","text":"learn to ask:"},{"type":"p","text":"\"Why does this problem exist within the larger system?\""},{"type":"p","text":"For example:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Plastic Waste","Consumer Behaviour","Packaging","Retail System","Collection","Recycling Infrastructure","Policy","Economic Incentives"]},{"type":"p","text":"This is particularly important for sustainable-design research."}]},{"heading":"Field Research","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Fieldwork should become a major part of the student's portfolio."},{"type":"p","text":"Potential research environments:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Villages"},{"text":"Urban communities"},{"text":"Schools"},{"text":"Hospitals"},{"text":"Public transport"},{"text":"Government services"},{"text":"Waste-management systems"},{"text":"Agriculture"},{"text":"Manufacturing"},{"text":"Retail"},{"text":"Non-profit organisations"},{"text":"Environmental projects"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Learn"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Field observation"},{"text":"Interview ethics"},{"text":"Participant consent"},{"text":"Research documentation"},{"text":"Stakeholder mapping"},{"text":"Community engagement"},{"text":"Participatory workshops"},{"text":"Research synthesis"}]}]},{"heading":"Year 4 — Strategic Design Research","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Year 4 should demonstrate professional-level research capability."},{"type":"h","text":"Advanced Areas"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Strategic research"},{"text":"Service design research"},{"text":"Systems research"},{"text":"Sustainability assessment"},{"text":"Behavioural research"},{"text":"Design evaluation"},{"text":"Research synthesis"},{"text":"Research storytelling"},{"text":"Stakeholder communication"},{"text":"Research-to-strategy translation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Final-Year Project"},{"type":"p","text":"A strong project could be:"},{"type":"h","text":"\"Design Research for Reducing Household Food Waste\""},{"type":"p","text":"Research:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Household behaviour"},{"text":"Shopping habits"},{"text":"Food storage"},{"text":"Consumption patterns"},{"text":"Waste generation"},{"text":"Existing interventions"},{"text":"Economic factors"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Then develop:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Field Research","User Behaviour","System Mapping","Key Insights","Opportunity Areas","Design Intervention","Prototype","User Testing","Impact Evaluation"]},{"type":"p","text":"The final project should demonstrate research leading to an evidence-based design decision."}]},{"heading":"Specialisation Options","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Specialisation","Key Focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"User Research"},{"text":"Understanding user behaviour"}],[{"text":"Social Research"},{"text":"Communities and social issues"}],[{"text":"Sustainability Research"},{"text":"Environmental challenges"}],[{"text":"Service Design Research"},{"text":"Services and customer journeys"}],[{"text":"Systems Research"},{"text":"Complex interconnected problems"}],[{"text":"UX Research"},{"text":"Digital products and users"}],[{"text":"Design Strategy Research"},{"text":"Research informing business/design strategy"}],[{"text":"Behavioural Research"},{"text":"Human decision-making"}],[{"text":"Inclusive Design Research"},{"text":"Accessibility and inclusion"}],[{"text":"Circular Design Research"},{"text":"Resource and material systems"}],[{"text":"Policy Design Research"},{"text":"Public systems and policy"}],[{"text":"Community-Based Research"},{"text":"Participatory community development"}]]}]},{"heading":"Research Tools","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Research & Documentation"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Notion"},{"text":"Miro"},{"text":"FigJam"},{"text":"Google Forms"},{"text":"Microsoft Forms"},{"text":"Airtable"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Qualitative Analysis"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn tools such as:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"NVivo"},{"text":"ATLAS.ti"},{"text":"MAXQDA"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Quantitative Analysis"},{"type":"p","text":"Start with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Excel"},{"text":"Google Sheets"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Then progress to:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"SPSS"},{"text":"R"},{"text":"Python"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A design researcher does not necessarily need advanced programming, but data literacy is increasingly valuable."},{"type":"h","text":"Design"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Figma"},{"text":"Adobe Illustrator"},{"text":"Photoshop"},{"text":"InDesign"}]}]},{"heading":"Research Portfolio","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The portfolio should not simply show attractive final designs."},{"type":"p","text":"It should show how evidence changed the design direction."},{"type":"h","text":"Project 1 — User Research"},{"type":"note","label":"Topic","text":"Public Transport Experience"},{"type":"p","text":"Include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Research question"},{"text":"Participant profile"},{"text":"Interviews"},{"text":"Observations"},{"text":"Affinity mapping"},{"text":"Insights"},{"text":"Recommendations"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Project 2 — Sustainability Research"},{"type":"note","label":"Topic","text":"Household Waste"},{"type":"p","text":"Include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Behaviour study"},{"text":"Waste journey"},{"text":"Stakeholder map"},{"text":"System map"},{"text":"Opportunity areas"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Project 3 — Community Research"},{"type":"note","label":"Topic","text":"Rural Service Access"},{"type":"p","text":"Include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Field research"},{"text":"Interviews"},{"text":"Community mapping"},{"text":"Pain points"},{"text":"Stakeholder ecosystem"},{"text":"Proposed intervention"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Project 4 — Service Research"},{"type":"note","label":"Topic","text":"Public Healthcare Service"},{"type":"p","text":"Map:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Awareness","Access","Registration","Waiting","Consultation","Treatment","Follow-up"]},{"type":"p","text":"Identify research-backed improvement opportunities."},{"type":"h","text":"Project 5 — Final Research Project"},{"type":"p","text":"Choose a substantial social or sustainability challenge and demonstrate the complete research-to-intervention process."}]},{"heading":"Internship Strategy","kind":"internships","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Target organisations such as:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Design research consultancies"},{"text":"UX research teams"},{"text":"Service design firms"},{"text":"Sustainability consultancies"},{"text":"Social innovation organisations"},{"text":"NGOs"},{"text":"Think tanks"},{"text":"Policy organisations"},{"text":"CSR teams"},{"text":"Design studios"},{"text":"Government innovation programmes"},{"text":"Research institutions"},{"text":"Circular-economy organisations"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Suitable Internship Roles"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Design Research Intern"},{"text":"UX Research Intern"},{"text":"Service Design Intern"},{"text":"Social Innovation Intern"},{"text":"Sustainability Research Intern"},{"text":"Research Assistant"},{"text":"Design Strategy Intern"},{"text":"User Research Intern"}]}]},{"heading":"Strong Internship Project","kind":"internships","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A particularly strong project would be:"},{"type":"h","text":"\"Understanding Urban Waste Behaviour\""},{"type":"p","text":"Research:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Interview households"},{"text":"Observe disposal behaviour"},{"text":"Study collection systems"},{"text":"Interview waste workers"},{"text":"Map stakeholders"},{"text":"Analyse behavioural patterns"},{"text":"Identify systemic barriers"},{"text":"Develop intervention opportunities"},{"text":"Prototype a solution"},{"text":"Test with users"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The final report should clearly distinguish:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Evidence","Pattern","Insight","Opportunity","Intervention","Evaluation"]}]},{"heading":"Certifications & Learning","kind":"certifications","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Useful areas include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Design thinking"},{"text":"User research"},{"text":"UX research"},{"text":"Service design"},{"text":"Systems thinking"},{"text":"Sustainability"},{"text":"Circular economy"},{"text":"ESG fundamentals"},{"text":"Sustainable development"},{"text":"Data analysis"},{"text":"Qualitative research"},{"text":"Human-centred design"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Certifications are useful for structured learning, but a well-documented research portfolio is more valuable than collecting many certificates."}]},{"heading":"Careers You Can Be Hired As","kind":"careers","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Possible entry-level positions include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Design Research Assistant"},{"text":"Junior Design Researcher"},{"text":"UX Researcher"},{"text":"User Researcher"},{"text":"Service Design Researcher"},{"text":"Social Innovation Researcher"},{"text":"Sustainability Research Assistant"},{"text":"Design Strategy Associate"},{"text":"Research Analyst"},{"text":"Behavioural Research Assistant"},{"text":"Innovation Research Associate"},{"text":"Community Research Associate"}]},{"type":"p","text":"With experience:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Design Researcher"},{"text":"Senior Design Researcher"},{"text":"Service Design Researcher"},{"text":"Strategic Researcher"},{"text":"Research Lead"},{"text":"Design Strategy Lead"}]}]},{"heading":"Interview Preparation","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Research Methods"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"What is design research?"},{"text":"What is the difference between qualitative and quantitative research?"},{"text":"How would you conduct a user interview?"},{"text":"How would you select research participants?"},{"text":"How do you avoid leading questions?"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Analysis"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"How do you convert interview data into insights?"},{"text":"What is affinity mapping?"},{"text":"What is qualitative coding?"},{"text":"How do you distinguish an observation from an insight?"},{"text":"How would you validate a research finding?"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Sustainability"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"What is circular design?"},{"text":"How can design contribute to sustainable behaviour?"},{"text":"How would you research a waste-management problem?"},{"text":"What is systems thinking?"},{"text":"How would you measure the impact of a sustainability intervention?"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Portfolio"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Explain your research question."},{"text":"Why did you choose your research method?"},{"text":"What surprised you during fieldwork?"},{"text":"How did your research change the design direction?"},{"text":"What would you investigate next?"}]}]},{"heading":"Postgraduate Options","kind":"pg_india","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Relevant postgraduate pathways include:"},{"type":"h","text":"Design"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"M.Des"},{"text":"M.Des in Design Research"},{"text":"M.Des in Service Design"},{"text":"M.Des in Strategic Design"},{"text":"M.Des in Social Design"},{"text":"M.Des in Sustainable Design"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Sustainability"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Sustainability Management"},{"text":"Environmental Design"},{"text":"Sustainable Development"},{"text":"Circular Economy"},{"text":"Environmental Management"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Research & Social Sciences"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Human-Computer Interaction"},{"text":"Sociology"},{"text":"Anthropology"},{"text":"Behavioural Science"},{"text":"Development Studies"},{"text":"Public Policy"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Management"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Design Management"},{"text":"Innovation Management"},{"text":"Sustainability Management"}]},{"type":"p","text":"For someone specifically targeting design research, a strong design-research/service-design postgraduate programme can be more directly aligned than a general management degree."}]},{"heading":"High-Value Specialist Routes","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Route A — Design Research"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Des","Research Internship","Research Assistant","Junior Design Researcher","Design Researcher","Senior Design Researcher","Research Lead"]},{"type":"h","text":"Route B — UX Research"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Des","Human-Centred Design","UX Research Internship","Junior UX Researcher","UX Researcher","Senior UX Researcher","UX Research Lead"]},{"type":"h","text":"Route C — Sustainability Research"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Des Sustainable Design","Sustainability Research Internship","Research Associate","Sustainability / Design Researcher","Senior Researcher","Sustainability Strategy Lead"]},{"type":"h","text":"Route D — Social Innovation"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Des","Community Research","Social Innovation Project","Innovation Researcher","Senior Social Innovation Researcher","Social Innovation / Strategy Lead"]}]},{"heading":"Research Ethics","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"This is particularly important for social and community research."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Informed consent"},{"text":"Participant privacy"},{"text":"Confidentiality"},{"text":"Responsible data collection"},{"text":"Avoiding researcher bias"},{"text":"Respect for vulnerable communities"},{"text":"Ethical photography/documentation"},{"text":"Responsible use of participant stories"},{"text":"Secure data handling"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A professional researcher should never treat communities simply as sources of information."}]},{"heading":"Measuring Design Impact","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Design Researcher should understand how to evaluate whether an intervention actually works."},{"type":"p","text":"Possible metrics:"},{"type":"h","text":"Social"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Participation"},{"text":"Accessibility"},{"text":"Inclusion"},{"text":"User satisfaction"},{"text":"Service adoption"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Environmental"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Waste reduction"},{"text":"Energy consumption"},{"text":"Material usage"},{"text":"Carbon impact"},{"text":"Product lifespan"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Behavioural"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Adoption rate"},{"text":"Behaviour change"},{"text":"Repeat usage"},{"text":"Engagement"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Economic"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Cost reduction"},{"text":"Resource efficiency"},{"text":"Revenue impact"},{"text":"Operational efficiency"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The researcher should establish:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Baseline","Intervention","Measurement","Comparison","Learning"]}]},{"heading":"AI & Future of Design Research","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"AI will increasingly support research activities such as:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Interview transcription"},{"text":"Qualitative data organisation"},{"text":"Pattern discovery"},{"text":"Survey analysis"},{"text":"Research synthesis"},{"text":"Literature analysis"},{"text":"Persona development"},{"text":"Scenario generation"},{"text":"Trend analysis"},{"text":"Data visualisation"}]},{"type":"p","text":"However, researchers still need to provide:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Research judgement"},{"text":"Context"},{"text":"Ethical reasoning"},{"text":"Human interpretation"},{"text":"Field understanding"},{"text":"Critical thinking"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A future-ready profile is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Design Research","Systems Thinking","Sustainability","Data Literacy","AI-Assisted Research"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"AI-generated patterns should always be validated against the underlying evidence rather than treated as automatically correct."}]},{"heading":"Study Abroad Directions","kind":"abroad","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Students can explore programmes related to:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Design Research"},{"text":"Strategic Design"},{"text":"Service Design"},{"text":"Social Design"},{"text":"Sustainable Design"},{"text":"Interaction Design"},{"text":"Human-Centred Design"},{"text":"Sustainability"},{"text":"Innovation"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Potential study destinations include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"UK"},{"text":"Netherlands"},{"text":"Germany"},{"text":"Denmark"},{"text":"Sweden"},{"text":"Finland"},{"text":"USA"},{"text":"Canada"},{"text":"Australia"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Program selection should be based on the research methodology, studio projects, fieldwork opportunities and industry collaborations, not only the programme title."}]},{"heading":"Career Progression","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"flow","items":["B.Des Graduate","Research Intern","Research Assistant / Junior Researcher","Design Researcher","Senior Design Researcher","Lead Design Researcher","Research Lead / Strategy Lead","Design Research Director"]},{"type":"p","text":"An alternative strategy-oriented path:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Design Researcher","Service Design Researcher","Strategic Design Researcher","Design Strategist","Strategy Lead"]}]},{"heading":"Recommended Final Skill Stack","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Research"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"User interviews"},{"text":"Observation"},{"text":"Ethnography"},{"text":"Surveys"},{"text":"Qualitative coding"},{"text":"Data analysis"},{"text":"Research synthesis"},{"text":"Research reporting"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Design"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Human-centred design"},{"text":"Service design"},{"text":"Systems thinking"},{"text":"Prototyping"},{"text":"Visualisation"},{"text":"Design strategy"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Sustainability"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Circular economy"},{"text":"Sustainable materials"},{"text":"Sustainable behaviour"},{"text":"Environmental systems"},{"text":"Impact measurement"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Technology"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Figma"},{"text":"Miro/FigJam"},{"text":"Excel"},{"text":"Qualitative analysis software"},{"text":"Basic statistics"},{"text":"Optional Python/R"},{"text":"AI research tools"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Professional"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Presentation"},{"text":"Facilitation"},{"text":"Stakeholder communication"},{"text":"Research ethics"},{"text":"Project management"},{"text":"Evidence-based decision-making"}]}]},{"heading":"Best Profile by Graduation","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A strong graduate profile should look like:"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Des Design for Social Innovation/Sustainable Design","Human-Centred Research","Qualitative & Quantitative Methods","Systems Thinking","Service Design","Sustainability Knowledge","Data Literacy","4–6 Research Projects","Field Research","Internship","Strong Research Portfolio"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Target progression"},{"type":"note","label":"Year 1","text":"Observation + design fundamentals\nYear 2: Research methods + user studies\nYear 3: Field research + systems/sustainability research\nYear 4: Strategic research + major social/sustainability project + internship\nAfter graduation: Research Assistant / Junior Design Researcher\n3–5 years: Design Researcher / UX or Service Researcher\n5–8 years: Senior Design Researcher / Strategic Researcher\n8+ years: Research Lead / Design Strategy Lead"},{"type":"note","label":"Key point","text":"The strongest candidate is not simply someone who can conduct interviews. They can identify the right research question, collect reliable evidence, synthesise complex information, uncover meaningful insights, connect those insights to design opportunities, and evaluate whether the resulting intervention creates measurable impact."}]}]}